<div class="row mb-2">
    <div class="col-12">
        <div class="card border-info shadow-sm">
            <div class="card-header bg-light text-primary fw-bold d-flex justify-content-between align-items-center">
                <span>
                    <i class="mdi mdi-information-outline me-2"></i> Overdraft Configuration Guidelines
                </span>
                <button class="btn btn-sm btn-outline-primary" type="button" data-bs-toggle="collapse" data-bs-target="#overdraftGuidelinesBody">
                    <i class="mdi mdi-chevron-down"></i>
                </button>
            </div>

            <div id="overdraftGuidelinesBody" class="collapse">
                <div class="card-body">
                    <ul class="mb-3 list-unstyled">

                        <!-- ✅ Eligibility -->
                        <li class="mb-2">
                            <i class="mdi mdi-shield-check-outline text-success me-2"></i>
                            <strong>Eligibility Rules:</strong> Define which account product the OD applies to. Set minimum credit score, salary linkage, and allowed member segments.
                        </li>

                        <!-- 💰 Limits -->
                        <li class="mb-2">
                            <i class="mdi mdi-percent-outline text-info me-2"></i>
                            <strong>Limit Calculations:</strong> OD limits can be based on salary percentage, income bands, or fixed default values. Legal and internal caps must both be respected.
                        </li>

                        <!-- 🧠 Interest -->
                        <li class="mb-2">
                            <i class="mdi mdi-chart-line text-dark me-2"></i>
                            <strong>Interest Strategy:</strong> Define a flat fee rate or use tiered interest based on utilization brackets (e.g., 0–50%, 51–100%). Tiers override the flat rate.
                        </li>

                        <!-- 💸 Disbursement -->
                        <li class="mb-2">
                            <i class="mdi mdi-bank-transfer-in text-primary me-2"></i>
                            <strong>Disbursement Behavior:</strong> Enable full or partial draws. OD can be auto-disbursed to a linked account. Exceeding limits can trigger additional fees or blocks.
                        </li>

                        <!-- 📅 Tenure & Expiry -->
                        <li class="mb-2">
                            <i class="mdi mdi-calendar-clock-outline text-secondary me-2"></i>
                            <strong>Tenure Control:</strong> Specify how long the OD is active (e.g., 90 days). You can set expiry dates and whether the OD is renewable after expiration.
                        </li>

                        <!-- 🔁 Replenishment -->
                        <li class="mb-2">
                            <i class="mdi mdi-autorenew text-warning me-2"></i>
                            <strong>Replenishment:</strong> Use the auto-replenishment frequency to refresh OD usage — monthly, quarterly, etc.
                        </li>

                        <!-- 💳 Repayment -->
                        <li class="mb-2">
                            <i class="mdi mdi-cash-refund text-success me-2"></i>
                            <strong>Recovery Logic:</strong> OD can be auto-recovered from incoming deposits or repaid manually. Grace period and delayed interest options are available.
                        </li>

                        <!-- ⬆️ Top-Ups -->
                        <li class="mb-2">
                            <i class="mdi mdi-cash-plus text-info me-2"></i>
                            <strong>Top-Up Requests:</strong> Members may request overdraft increases, subject to a top-up fee and configured maximums.
                        </li>

                        <!-- 🔔 Notifications -->
                        <li class="mb-2">
                            <i class="mdi mdi-bell-alert-outline text-primary me-2"></i>
                            <strong>Notifications:</strong> Notify members when OD usage reaches a defined percentage threshold. Useful for monitoring and self-control.
                        </li>

                        <!-- 💼 Income Tiering -->
                        <li class="mb-2">
                            <i class="mdi mdi-account-cash-outline text-teal me-2"></i>
                            <strong>Income-Based OD:</strong> Use limit bands to assign OD amounts based on income ranges (e.g. 0–100k, 100k–250k).
                        </li>

                        <!-- ⚠️ Penalties -->
                        <li class="mb-2">
                            <i class="mdi mdi-alert-circle-outline text-danger me-2"></i>
                            <strong>Penalty Enforcement:</strong> Associate penalty rules for overdraft misuse, late repayment, or limit breaches. These are enforced at runtime if enabled.
                        </li>

                        <!-- ⚠️ Risk -->
                        <li class="mb-2">
                            <i class="mdi mdi-alert-outline text-danger me-2"></i>
                            <strong>Important:</strong> Misconfigured overdraft settings may block legitimate usage or create financial risk. Always validate values before enabling.
                        </li>
                    </ul>

                    <hr class="my-3" />

                    <p class="text-muted mb-0">
                        <i class="mdi mdi-help-circle-outline me-2"></i>
                        For compliance, legal, or credit policy guidance, consult your internal control or risk department before applying changes to active overdraft products.
                    </p>
                </div>
            </div>
        </div>
    </div>
</div>
